class.description:
A [VideoPreset] bundles the values that [method VideoPresetSettingsServer.apply_preset] sets in the settings domains [code]"video_quality"[/code] ([VideoQualitySettingsServer]), [code]"video_texture"[/code] ([VideoTextureSettingsServer]), [code]"video_shadow"[/code] ([VideoShadowSettingsServer]) and [code]"video_effect"[/code] ([VideoEffectSettingsServer]). Each domain has a [Dictionary] that maps the name of a setting (see [method SettingsServer.get_setting_names]) to its value. A preset holds only the values it sets; the other values of a domain keep the value they have, so a preset can be partial. Enum values are stored as their integer value.
The four built-in presets are created with [method VideoPresetSettingsServer.create_builtin_preset]. To replace or add presets, save a [VideoPreset] as a [code].tres[/code] file and add it to [member ProjectSettings.settings/video_preset/presets], or call [method VideoPresetSettingsServer.add_preset] at runtime. The window settings ([VideoWindowSettingsServer]) are not part of a preset.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var preset = VideoPresetSettingsServer.create_builtin_preset("High")
preset.preset_name = "Cinematic"
preset.set_value("video_effect", "dof_blur_quality", RenderingServer.DOF_BLUR_QUALITY_HIGH)
preset.set_value("video_quality", "scaling_3d_scale", 1.5)
VideoPresetSettingsServer.add_preset(preset)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
VideoPreset preset = VideoPresetSettingsServer.CreateBuiltinPreset("High");
preset.PresetName = "Cinematic";
preset.SetValue("video_effect", "dof_blur_quality", (int)RenderingServer.DofBlurQuality.High);
preset.SetValue("video_quality", "scaling_3d_scale", 1.5);
VideoPresetSettingsServer.AddPreset(preset);
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] Use values a domain accepts unchanged (for example powers of two for shadow atlas sizes). A value the domain clamps or rounds no longer matches the preset after it is applied, so the next change of any value of the preset shows [code]"Custom"[/code].
